proteus (0.4.2~beta-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * v0.4.2-beta — second beta in the v0.4 cycle. Closes the remainder of
    the May 2026 audit tree (#279, #285-306 cluster) plus three audit
    follow-up findings (PROTEUS_*_DIR env-var lockdown, iface validation
    on ethtool/iw, iw/ip `--` defense-in-depth) carried over from the
    SECURITY-AUDIT-2026-05-07-followup doc.
  * Persona export safety parity (--yes / symlink-check / atomic-write /
    refuse-overwrite). Quarantine no longer destroys originals on entry.
  * Cross-layer persona consistency (DHCP opt-55, mDNS records, TCP
    fingerprint hints) for brand-named stealth personas.
  * Default rotation cadence randomized to break the v0.3.x recognizable
    "every-2h-on-the-hour ±5min" Proteus signature.
  * Code quality: SHA-256 deduplicated to a single canonical
    implementation; status feature_table corrected; completions
    regenerated; uninstall/quarantine env-var lockdown.
  * Packaging: dropped clashing dist/debian/compat (debhelper-compat is
    in Build-Depends). RPM %systemd_post enables proteus-boot.service.
  * Docs: professional clean-and-polish pass over wiki, README, dist
    READMEs, and code comments. Stale phase markers removed.

